A small note, there is now a version in English too at 
http://www.nada.kth.se/~nv89-nun/omega-us.html

The mailing list is however in Swedish. Which hopefully will induce
a small evolution-encouraging barrier between the list and other
similar lists. Strength through diversity. 


Andre asked:

>Please explain to me what is Transhumanism.

Quoted from the Extropian FAQ:

"Transhumanism 
 Philosophies of life (such as the Extropian philosophy) that seek the
 continuation and acceleration of the evolution of intelligent life beyond its
 currently human form and limits by means of science and technology, guided
 by life-promoting principles and values, while avoiding religion and 
 dogma."


Extropianism can be viewed as a libertarian subset of transhumanism. 
Before starting the list we discussed whether or not to call it an
Extropian list, but I convinced the others that its better to be
more general that to bind ourselves to a single transhumanist
philosophy. However, quite naturally there seems to be a libertarian
slant on the list anyway (really simple memetics, statist memes have
a hard time coping with the vision of transhumanism, since they are
essentially linked to steady-state systems). 
 
